5.2 What I Learned from This Project
Building this project taught me how to break a large python application into clean, reusable modular files rather than writing one gigantic script. I learned the power of smart algorithmic choices—like filtering by file size before computing heavy SHA-256 hashes—which makes duplicate detection lightning fast. I also experienced how background threading (`threading.Thread`) keeps a user interface smooth and responsive while heavy scanning happens behind the scenes. Most importantly, I realized that writing code that touches real files requires a safe, non-destructive mindset, using dry-run previews, collision renaming, quarantine folders, and instant undo actions so users never lose their precious memories.